guid> </item> <item> <title>Authentication</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Authentication&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Below are examples of the available authentication methods.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Certificates&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;```yamlenvironment: host: my-sense-instance.com port: 42...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/authentication/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/authentication/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/authentication/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Commands</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Commands&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h2&gt;List of the available commands and their description&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3&gt;file&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;The runbook file location&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;!!! example &#34;Example&#34;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;`automatiqal --file path...&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/commands/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/commands/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/commands/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Examples</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Examples&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;For runbook examples please check:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/Informatiqal/automatiqal-cli/tree/main/runbook-examples&#34;&gt;Automatiqal CLI Tests&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;[Auto...&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/examples/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/examples/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/examples/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Initial checks</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Initial checks&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Automatiqal&lt;/code&gt; will perform few initial checks &lt;strong&gt;before start running&lt;/strong&gt; the tasks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If any of these checks fails then the process will exit ...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/initial-checks/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/initial-checks/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/initial-checks/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Installation</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Install&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Installation is quite simple:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm install -g automatiqal-cli&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Once the installation is complete just run:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;automatiqal --help&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;To verify that...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/install/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/install/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/install/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Multiple environments</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Multiple environments&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;The default behavior of the runbook is &#34;one runbook one environment&#34;. Usually this is more than enough but there are cases where the...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/multiple-environments/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/multiple-environments/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/multiple-environments/</guid> </item> <item> <title>onError block</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;OnError&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Each task can have a &lt;code&gt;try ... catch&lt;/code&gt; workflow defined.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;onError&lt;/code&gt; block is just a list of tasks to be performed if &lt;code&gt;Automatiqal&lt;/code&gt; encounter an ...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/on-error-block/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/on-error-block/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/on-error-block/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Output</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Outputs&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Two output related flags are available:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Output&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;When this flag is used the raw output will be saved as json format in the provided file name:...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/output/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/output/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/output/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Runbook structure</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Runbook structure&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;The runbook have 3 main parts:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#header&#34;&gt;Header&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#environment&#34;&gt;Environment&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#tasks&#34;&gt;Tasks&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Header&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;```yamlname: Sample run...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/runbook-structure/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/runbook-structure/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/runbook-structure/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Schema</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Schema&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Great little addition is the availability of &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/Informatiqal/automatiqal-cli-schema&#34;&gt;YAML schema&lt;/a&gt;. The schema greatly helps when w...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/schema/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/schema/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/schema/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Conditions</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Conditions&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Apart from &lt;code&gt;skip&lt;/code&gt; property, which have to be set explicitly, tasks can be skipped based on condition. &lt;code&gt;when&lt;/code&gt; condition can be set for tasks and...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/conditions/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/conditions/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/conditions/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Filter/source</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Filter/source&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;When working with existing entities in QMC (apps, streams, reload tasks, virtual proxies etc.) we can use &lt;code&gt;filter&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;source&lt;/code&gt; task property to...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/filter-source/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/filter-source/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/filter-source/</guid> </item> </channel></rss>